<h1>Rooted in Christ (RiC) — Technical Baseline</h1>
<p><em>Discovery pass only. No code was changed. No secrets are included.</em></p>

<h2>Executive Summary</h2>
<p>RiC today is a single <strong>Vite + React 19 SPA</strong> with all application logic in the browser. It ships a public-domain KJV corpus locally and layers YouVersion Platform content on top through a mix of the official <code>@youversion</code> SDK and a custom REST wrapper. User state lives in <code>localStorage</code> + <code>IndexedDB</code> and syncs to Firebase Auth + Firestore. A Capacitor Android wrapper exists but is a packaged WebView. The network graph, geography, and people/timeline features are implemented on hand-curated, hard-coded starter datasets and rule-based algorithms.</p>
<p><strong>The honest bottom line:</strong> the prototype proves the product vision, but it is still a prototype. The KJV reader and search work today; the YouVersion reader works if the auth callback is fixed; the visual features are compelling demos; and the data layer is almost entirely local and hand-maintained.</p>

