<h2>PART 3 — Current Bible Data Pipeline</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Source:</strong> <code>public/data/kjv_raw.json</code> is the structured KJV; <code>scripts/transform.mjs</code> flattens it to <code>public/data/bible.json</code> (31,102 verses).</li>
<li><strong>Provenance:</strong> README states KJV was downloaded from <code>midvash/bible-data</code>; KJV is public domain in the US.</li>
<li><strong>Loading:</strong> <code>bible.ts</code> fetches <code>/data/bible.json</code> via <code>fetchCachedJson</code> in <code>indexedStorage.ts</code>; <code>App.tsx</code> loads Bible, places, and characters on mount.</li>
<li><strong>Indexing:</strong> <code>bible.ts</code> builds Fuse.js index for text, bookName, book; a <code>wordIndex</code> for instant single-word lookup; and <code>bookFuse</code> for book names.</li>
<li><strong>Search:</strong> <code>searchBible()</code> handles references, natural-language questions, exact phrases, and fuzzy fallback.</li>
<li><strong>Reader display:</strong> YouVersion versions are fetched as HTML, transformed with <code>@youversion/platform-core</code>, then red-letter and named-entity markup is applied. Local KJV text powers search, map, network, and sidebar.</li>
</ul>

<h2>PART 4 — Current YouVersion Integration</h2>
<p><strong>YouVersion is integrated.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><code>youversion.ts</code> is a custom REST client for <code>/bibles</code>, <code>/passages/{usfm}</code>, <code>/languages</code>, legacy search, and audio.</li>
<li><code>AuthGate.tsx</code> and <code>App.tsx</code> use the <code>@youversion</code> SDK (Provider, hooks) for auth and data.</li>
<li>What works: listing versions/books/chapters, fetching passage HTML, searching, audio, split-translation compare mode, version selection.</li>
<li>What does not: <strong>YouVersion Sign-In fails with “redirect_uri does not match registered callback URL.”</strong> <code>youversionRedirect.ts</code> computes the redirect from <code>window.location.origin</code> or <code>VITE_YVP_REDIRECT_URL</code>. The mismatch is in the YouVersion console callback registration, which is not in the repo.</li>
</ul>

