<h2>PART 17 — Architectural Assessment</h2>
<h3>KEEP</h3>
<ul>
<li>Local KJV as offline fallback.</li>
<li><code>bible.ts</code> indexing and search pattern for KJV.</li>
<li><code>Place</code>/<code>Character</code>/<code>PassageMatch</code> shapes and matching logic.</li>
<li>Visual network graph concept and WebGL renderer.</li>
<li>Light/dark theme and CSS variables.</li>
<li>en/es i18n scaffold.</li>
</ul>
<h3>REFACTOR</h3>
<ul>
<li><code>App.tsx</code> and <code>YouVersionReaderTab.tsx</code> are too large; split into feature modules.</li>
<li>Data layer should be abstracted behind a <code>BibleClient</code> / <code>BibleService</code>.</li>
<li><code>storage.ts</code> should be wrapped in a clean repository/adapter pattern.</li>
</ul>
<h3>REPLACE</h3>
<ul>
<li>Rule-based cross-reference scoring with a real cross-reference dataset + semantic model.</li>
<li>Hand-curated <code>places.json</code>/<code>characters.json</code> with licensed/expanded datasets.</li>
<li>Rule-based “AI insight” with RAG/LLM.</li>
<li>localStorage-only persistence with a proper backend.</li>
</ul>
<h3>CONNECT TO YOUTUBEERSION</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Capability</th><th>Use</th></tr>
<tr><td>Auth (Sign-In / OAuth / PKCE)</td><td>Official SDK</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bible / version / passage content</td><td>REST API or SDK hooks</td></tr>
<tr><td>Search</td><td>REST API</td></tr>
<tr><td>User highlights / bookmarks</td><td>Data Exchange API where permitted</td></tr>
<tr><td>Audio</td><td>REST API</td></tr>
</table>
<h3>BUILD OURSELVES</h3>
<ul>
<li>RiC Scripture Graph / Hyperlink Matrix.</li>
<li>Integrated biblical geography and timeline.</li>
<li>RAG + AI study companion.</li>
<li>Canonical Scripture reference layer across versification systems.</li>
</ul>
<h3>DO NOT BUILD</h3>
<ul>
<li>User auth (Firebase / YouVersion already provide it).</li>
<li>Bible content CDN / version management (YouVersion).</li>
<li>Audio streaming (YouVersion).</li>
<li>Copyright-compliant translation distribution (YouVersion).</li>
</ul>

